{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuijHTUjAFHEQdRArsN2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It depends on your Wrangler version and how you write the config. Recent Wrangler 4.x releases (from about late 2025) can provision KV namespaces automatically. If you declare a `kv_namespaces` binding with only a `binding` name and no `id`, `wrangler deploy` creates the namespace and attaches it. If you give an `id`, it must point to a namespace that already exists. Older versions never create KV namespaces, so you'd run `wrangler kv namespace create <NAME>` first.\n\nAs far as I know, queues aren't created automatically. If a producer or consumer binding names a queue that doesn't exist, the deploy fails and tells you to run `wrangler queues create <name>`. I answered from memory without checking current docs, so confirm with `wrangler --version` and the Cloudflare docs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5820,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5820},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11e5935c-af19-4668-8e50-4965a2b60875","uuid":"1b0f0efa-dd62-4fe9-932a-883a1bf82a4d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:13:38.210Z","request_id":"req_011CfuijHEqBZqWWuiU62UCi"}
